Z||000004||SloPonti||09-27-1999||10:28 PM||||why do you say bad news? fill us in here! my car runs just fine though! like the guy said before me i do know that it is coming through the valve cover filter into the air intake but i do not know why! help us out!!!||||reg||5
Z||000005||Shiner||09-27-1999||10:31 PM||||Replace the PCV valve, and go ahead and replace the PCV filter.  My '84 had the same problem (not quite as bas as yours) and it cured it compleatly.||||reg||3
Z||000006||Eddie||09-27-1999||10:43 PM||||It was valve that whent on my 87 2.5.  I could hear the valve at high rpms  soon after it was all over the lefter cracked . HAVE IT CHECKED<BR>OIL SHOULD NEVER REACH THE AIR FILTER||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||09-27-1999||11:57 PM||||replace the PCV valve as a start. it's a cheap part. Replace the filter as well. You can likely get both at wall mart. If you still blow oil after that, the engine is worn and it's going to blow oil untill you rebuild it or it breaks. Also try changing the oil.... it can help reduce the problem.<P>Note! 87+ 4 Cyl uses Fram breather filter BA3803 or equivalent. Many parts books are wrong for 87-88. If the book points you to a round filter try looking up 1987 Olds Cutlass Ciera with the same motor.<P>make sure the vacuum line from the PCV valve is clear. check the port on/under the TBI and make sure it's clear.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-28-1999).]||||reg||4
Z||000008||SloPonti||09-28-1999||06:13 PM||||i will replace the pcv valve and filter and let you know what happens! i do not think it has anything to do with the lifters or rocker arms though because i hear no odd noises from them and the car runs great! i let you know what happens!!!<BR>thanks||||reg||6
Z||000009||batboy||09-28-1999||10:43 PM||||There is a slight chance the PCV is defective, but more than likely, the oil in the air cleaner is caused from blow-by which means excessive piston ring and/or cylinder wear. I've owned lots of old high mileage "clunkers" in the past and this is common with an oil burning engine. If you are adding oil between changes and it's not leaking, then you're burning oil. This means the motor is wearing out. Simple as that.||||reg||1
